.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Uses \f[CR]MSG_PEEK\f[R] so the byte remains in the socket buffer for
the protocol handler to read normally.
.IP \(bu 2
The function only works on socket file descriptors (not pipes or regular
files) because it uses \f[CR]recv(2)\f[R] with \f[CR]MSG_PEEK\f[R].
For \f[CR]\-\-stdio\f[R] mode, a different detection path may be needed.
.IP \(bu 2
The detection is deterministic after a single byte, making it zero\-cost
for protocol negotiation.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]first_byte\f[R] output is primarily useful for debugging; the
return value is the authoritative protocol indicator.
